# Nine components, rendered

:::box{class=lead}
Every built-in the language ships, each one beside the source that produced it. Nothing here is
a screenshot — this page is a HyMarkX document, so the right-hand half of each pair is the
component itself, compiled by the same compiler you would run.
:::

:::note[This page pays for what it shows]{type=info}
The last three components exist so that interactivity has native elements to attach to, so this
page compiles in `app` trust and ships the runtime. The [documentation](/docs) does not, and
ships no JavaScript at all — same site, same compiler, different bill. The state for the live
example is declared once at the top of this document, because a declaration is only legal in a
document root.
:::

::::

::::box{as=section class="chapter reveal" #note}

:::box{class=eyebrow}
Container · label optional
:::

## note

:::box{class=lead}
A callout for something related to the prose but not part of it. `type` picks one of four
statuses; the label in square brackets becomes the heading, and a note without one is still a
note.
:::

| Attribute | Type | Default | Accepts |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `type` | enum | `info` | `info`, `warning`, `danger`, `success` |

::::box{class=example}

:::box{class=pane}
### Source

```md
:::note[Heads up]{type=warning}
Deployment starts at 8 PM UTC.
:::

:::note[Shipped]{type=success}
0.0.9 is on npm.
:::

:::note[Breaking]{type=danger}
`--fragment` replaces the old default.
:::

:::note
A note with no label at all.
:::
```
:::

:::box{class=preview}
### Rendered

:::note[Heads up]{type=warning}
Deployment starts at 8 PM UTC.
:::

:::note[Shipped]{type=success}
0.0.9 is on npm.
:::

:::note[Breaking]{type=danger}
`--fragment` replaces the old default.
:::

:::note
A note with no label at all.
:::
:::

::::

