::::box{as=section class="chapter reveal" #card}

:::box{class=eyebrow}
Container · label optional
:::

## card

:::box{class=lead}
A grouped block of content. The label becomes an `h3`, which keeps a page of cards navigable by
heading rather than by shape.
:::

::::box{class=example}

:::box{class=pane}
### Source

```md
:::card[Quarterly report]
Revenue rose in every region except EMEA.
:::
```
:::

:::box{class=preview}
### Rendered

:::card[Quarterly report]
Revenue rose in every region except EMEA.
:::
:::

::::

::::

::::box{as=section class="chapter reveal" #grid}

:::box{class=eyebrow}
Container · label optional
:::

## grid

:::box{class=lead}
Columns, for the one case Markdown cannot express. Both attributes are bounded integers, and
both are emitted as custom properties rather than as classes, so a host stylesheet can override
them at any breakpoint.
:::

| Attribute | Type | Default | Accepts |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `columns` | number | `3` | `1` through `12` |
| `gap` | number | `4` | `0` through `16` |

::::box{class=example}

:::box{class=pane}
### Source

```md
:::grid{columns=3 gap=3}
:::card[Parse]
micromark extensions, no regex.
:::
:::card[Analyse]
Schemas, spans, diagnostics.
:::
:::card[Emit]
Only what the document used.
:::
:::
```
:::

:::box{class=preview}
### Rendered

:::grid{columns=3 gap=3}
:::card[Parse]
micromark extensions, no regex.
:::
:::card[Analyse]
Schemas, spans, diagnostics.
:::
:::card[Emit]
Only what the document used.
:::
:::
:::

